WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
(solemn music)

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.040
- [Voiceover] Dear Mom,

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.999
these are the flowers
I would have bought you

00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:12.849
and this is the card I
would have written you.

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:19.012
I've spent most of my life
trying to fill in the blanks.

00:00:19.012 --> 00:00:20.933
Asking everyone around me about you.

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:24.712
The memories of you tucked
away in a box in the attic.

00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:26.893
I don't remember what
your perfume smelled like,

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.133
or what made you laugh,

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.232
but I'll never forget
lying in your hospital bed

00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:32.773
drawing pictures with you.

00:00:32.773 --> 00:00:34.993
Your rebellious little six year old.

00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:38.268
I'm writing this because I wanna tell you

00:00:38.268 --> 00:00:39.955
that you were so strong.

00:00:39.955 --> 00:00:41.475
That I wish you didn't have
to look at your daughter

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:43.335
knowing that you'd never
see her get taller,

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:44.795
get heartbroken, get married.

00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:47.783
I'm sorry that I always
made you pick me up

00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:49.523
when you were so weak.

00:00:49.523 --> 00:00:51.143
That I tripped over your IV pole.

00:00:52.353 --> 00:00:55.524
The Christmas I complained that
I didn't get what I wanted.

00:00:55.524 --> 00:00:57.185
Being afraid of your wig.

00:00:57.185 --> 00:00:59.008
I'm sorry for the fits I threw,

00:00:59.008 --> 00:01:01.158
the I love you moms I never got to say.

00:01:02.118 --> 00:01:03.722
And I'm sorry that it's taken me 21 years

00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:06.202
to write this card, and
it's still not perfect.

00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:09.169
I'm writing this because I'd give anything

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.889
just to be able to fight with you.

00:01:10.889 --> 00:01:12.949
I never got to ignore your phone calls

00:01:12.949 --> 00:01:14.585
because you were too overbearing.

00:01:14.585 --> 00:01:16.245
I never got to introduce
you to girlfriends

00:01:16.245 --> 00:01:17.972
or boyfriends you say are bad for me,

00:01:17.972 --> 00:01:19.492
and I tell you that you don't understand,

00:01:19.492 --> 00:01:22.152
but months later I realize
that you were right.

00:01:23.602 --> 00:01:24.892
I'm writing this because I'm angry

00:01:24.892 --> 00:01:27.313
that I have to live life only part way.

00:01:27.313 --> 00:01:29.013
All the yearbook pictures I took

00:01:29.013 --> 00:01:30.692
without you to do my hair,

00:01:30.692 --> 00:01:33.193
the lunches I made myself.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:36.073
I feel like I'm missing out on
a huge part of being a woman

00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:37.793
because you're not here.

00:01:37.793 --> 00:01:39.812
Like a part of me is in
that coffin with you,

00:01:39.812 --> 00:01:40.832
holding onto your leg,

00:01:40.832 --> 00:01:43.992
while I scoot across the
floor begging you not to go.

00:01:45.812 --> 00:01:47.513
You were so beautiful.

00:01:47.513 --> 00:01:49.492
It's insane to believe that anyone

00:01:49.492 --> 00:01:52.473
as beautiful as you ever
existed on this earth.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.332
I'm writing this because
I wish you were here,

00:01:56.332 --> 00:01:58.952
I wish you could see the
woman that I've grown into.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.393
I wish I knew which flowers you liked

00:02:00.393 --> 00:02:01.912
and that I could put them in your hands,

00:02:01.912 --> 00:02:04.413
rather than on a plot of
grass with your name on it.

00:02:05.863 --> 00:02:09.213
I'm writing this because
I wanna say thank you.

00:02:09.213 --> 00:02:11.592
No matter how sick you
were all you wanted to do

00:02:11.592 --> 00:02:13.753
was make sure I felt loved.

00:02:13.753 --> 00:02:15.992
Thank you for taking me to Disney World

00:02:15.992 --> 00:02:17.693
when you were in a wheelchair,

00:02:17.693 --> 00:02:20.053
letting me draw those
pictures in your hospital bed,

00:02:20.053 --> 00:02:21.873
writing me letters like you knew

00:02:21.873 --> 00:02:23.952
I'd grow up to be who I am.

00:02:23.952 --> 00:02:27.152
Making me feel like I was
so special and so smart.

00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:34.813
I feel like I'll always
be that six year old

00:02:34.813 --> 00:02:35.873
with a mind of her own,

00:02:35.873 --> 00:02:37.852
that didn't take orders
and doesn't wear dresses.

00:02:37.852 --> 00:02:39.392
That's still waiting
for her mom to wake up

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.492
and tell her that
everything is okay again.

00:02:43.502 --> 00:02:45.352
I'm writing this because
I'll never love anyone

00:02:45.352 --> 00:02:47.092
as much as I miss you.

00:02:47.092 --> 00:02:49.152
Happy Mother's Day.

